  "description": "Decode optimal tag sequence sequentially using emission potentials and state-to-state transition matrix.\n\nCRFs model structured label dependencies globally, preventing label bias problems inherent in independent per-token softmax classifications.\n\n### Mathematical Formulation\n$$\ny_t = \\arg\\max_{k} \\left[ \\psi_{\\text{emit}}(t, k) + \\psi_{\\text{trans}}(y_{t-1}, k) \\right]\n$$\n\n### Step-by-Step Implementation\n1. Initialize first tag y_0 maximizing initial emission potentials\n2. Iterate over timesteps t accumulating transition score from prev_tag plus current emission\n3. Select greedily optimal tag at each step\n\n### Returns\nList of integer tag indices.",
  "theory": "## Understanding the Theory: Greedy Sequence Tagging\n\n### Core Intuition: Why Do We Need This?\nNatural language consists of discrete words and symbols arranged in sequential order. To process text with neural networks, we convert words into continuous embedding vectors and model their grammatical and semantic relationships. **Greedy Sequence Tagging** is a core sequence-processing mechanism used in modern Transformer and LLM architectures.\n\nCRFs model structured label dependencies globally, preventing label bias problems inherent in independent per-token softmax classifications. In this problem, the goal is to: decode optimal tag sequence sequentially using emission potentials and state-to-state transition matrix.\n\n### Mathematical Principles & Formulation\nThe core governing equation for this operation is:\n\n$$\ny_t = \\arg\\max_{k} \\left[ \\psi_{\\text{emit}}(t, k) + \\psi_{\\text{trans}}(y_{t-1}, k) \\right]\n$$\n\nEvery term in this formulation plays a precise mathematical role in ensuring dimensional consistency, numerical stability, and correct algorithmic behavior.\n\n### Step-by-Step Computational Workflow\n1. **Phase 1**: Initialize first tag y_0 maximizing initial emission potentials\n2. **Phase 2**: Iterate over timesteps t accumulating transition score from prev_tag plus current emission\n3. **Phase 3**: Select greedily optimal tag at each step\n\n### Practical Machine Learning Applications & Nuances\n* **Self-Attention Mechanics**: Scaled dot-product attention computes all-to-all token interactions dynamically, allowing tokens to gather context from the entire sentence simultaneously.\n* **Position Encodings**: Because self-attention is permutation-invariant, positional encodings (like sinusoidal or Rotary Position Embeddings) inject word order into the representations.\n* **Vocabulary & Subwords**: Algorithms like BPE tokenize text into frequent subwords, allowing models to represent rare words without requiring an infinite vocabulary.",
  "examples": [
    "Input: emissions = [[2.0, 1.0], [0.5, 1.5], [2.0, 0.5]], transitions = [[1.0, 0.5], [0.2, 1.2]]\n\nOutput: [0, 1, 0]\n\nExplanation: Evaluated nlp_crf_layer under standard test conditions."
