  "starterCode": "import numpy as np\n\ndef nlp_crf_layer(emissions: list, transitions: list) -> list:\n    pass",
  "solution": "### 💡 Intuition & Approach\nThe implementation computes **Greedy Sequence Tagging** by following direct mathematical principles, leveraging vectorized operations to ensure both correctness and optimal runtime efficiency.\n\n### ⚡ Python Reference Implementation\n```python\nimport numpy as np\n\ndef nlp_crf_layer(emissions: list, transitions: list) -> list:\n    tags = [int(np.argmax(emissions[0]))]\n    for t in range(1, len(emissions)):\n        p = tags[-1]\n        tags.append(int(np.argmax([emissions[t][k] + transitions[p][k] for k in range(len(emissions[0]))])))\n    return tags\n```\n\n### ⏱️ Complexity Analysis\n- **Time Complexity**: $\\mathcal{O}(N)$ where $N$ represents the size of the primary input.\n- **Space Complexity**: $\\mathcal{O}(N)$ auxiliary memory for computing and storing output representations.",
